I converted `/data/users.csv` to a JSON array with `jq`, one object per row, using the header names (`name`, `age`, `city`) as keys:

```json
[
  {
    "name": "alice",
    "age": "30",
    "city": "seattle"
  },
  {
    "name": "bob",
    "age": "25",
    "city": "portland"
  },
  {
    "name": "charlie",
    "age": "35",
    "city": "denver"
  }
]
```

All values come out as strings, including `age` (`"30"` rather than `30`). The command splits each line on commas, so it would break on quoted fields that contain commas. This file has none.
